What is an Unattended Robot?
Easy Understanding

An Unattended Robot is a software robot that performs tasks automatically without any human intervention.

It works in the background and can execute tasks based on schedules or triggers.

Examples
Processing invoices
Generating reports
Updating databases
Sending emails
Real-Life Example

Suppose every day at 9 PM a company receives 500 invoices.

Instead of an employee manually:

Opening invoices
Extracting data
Updating database
Sending confirmation email

An unattended robot performs all these steps automatically without anyone logging in or clicking anything.

--------------------------
Components Used

UiPath Studio
Used to create automation workflows.
Design the automation process.

UiPath Orchestrator
Used to manage, monitor, deploy and schedule robots.
Controls robot execution.

----------------------------

2. Deployment of an Unattended Robot


Step 1: Create Automation Workflow

Using UiPath Studio, create the automation process.

Example: Invoice Processing Bot.

Exam Point

Design automation activities using UiPath Studio.

Step 2: Test the Workflow

Check whether the workflow works correctly.

Activities:

Execute workflow
Debug errors
Handle exceptions
Exam Point

The workflow is executed and tested for debugging and exception handling.

Step 3: Publish the Automation Project

Convert the developed project into a deployable package.

Exam Point

The automation project is published as a package for deployment.

Step 4: Provision and Connect Unattended Robot

Configure:

Machine
Robot
User credentials

Connect robot with Orchestrator.

Exam Point

The unattended robot is provisioned and connected to Orchestrator.

Step 5: Create Process in Orchestrator

Import the published package into Orchestrator.

Configure process settings.

Exam Point

A process is created using the published package.

Step 6: Execute Job

Orchestrator assigns the process to the robot.

Robot starts execution.

Exam Point

Orchestrator triggers the job and assigns tasks to the robot.

Step 7: Schedule Automation

Set:

Daily execution
Weekly execution
Trigger-based execution
Exam Point

Triggers are configured for automatic execution.



